le to tune their effective coupling strength. This allowed us to measure the effect of such a controllable and well-characterized environment on the qubit coherence. We can quantitatively account for our data with a simple model in which thermal fluctuations of the photon number in the oscillator are the limiting factor. In particular, we observe a strong reduction of the dephasing rate whenever the coupling is tuned to zero. At the optimal point we find a large spin-echo decay time of 4  μs.Received 19 July 2005DOI:https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.95.257002©2005 American Physical Society", "abstract_source_suggest": {"input": "APS"}}], "refereed": true, "titles": [{"source": "APS", "title": "Dephasing of a Superconducting Qubit Induced by Photon Noise"}], "facet_author_name": ["1949534_David P. DiVincenzo", "1953347_Kouichi Semba", "1971768_Guido Burkard", "2057140_I. Chiorescu", "2059589_Patrice Bertet", "2428224_J.E. Mooij", "2560372_C.J.P.M. Harmans"], "core": true, "imprints": [{"date": "2005-12-13"}], "_oai": {"sets": ["Literature"], "id": "oai:inspirehep.net:2792188", "updated": "2026-02-09T13:59:45.172408"}, "curated": true, "journal_title_variants": ["Phys. Rev. Lett.", "Phys.Rev.Lett."]}, "created": "2024-06-01T10:01:31.858602+00:00", "updated": "2026-02-09T13:59:45.172408+00:00", "links": {"bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2792188?format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2792188?format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2792188?format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2792188?format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2792188?format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2792188?format=cv", "citations": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A2792188"}, "id": "2792188"}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.95.257002&size=5&page=